cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. The surname is Amichis Luengo (two surnames, in this order)."
title: "The Watermark and Double Ladder Theorems (Verified in Lean)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Amichis Luengo"
    given-names: "Rafael"
    email: "tretoef@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Madrid, Spain"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tretoef-estrella/watermark-theorem"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: 2026-09-30
abstract: "For the complex Fermat surface of prime degree m >= 5, the lattice spanned by its 3m^2 lines has discriminant m^(3(m-3)^2) (the Watermark Theorem) and discriminant group (Z/m)^(3m^2-24m+59) x (Z/m^2)^(3m-16) for m >= 7, (Z/5)^10 x Z/25 for m = 5 (the Double Ladder Theorem). Both are proved, and certified in Lean 4 with Mathlib."
keywords:
  - Fermat surface
  - Néron–Severi lattice
  - discriminant
  - discriminant group
  - lines on surfaces
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formal verification
